,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,9,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,9,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,9,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7],[7,8,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,8,7],[7,8,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7],[7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7]],"output":[[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,9,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,9,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,8,7,7,9,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,8,7,7,9,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,8,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,8],[7,8,7,7,8,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7],[7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7],[7,8,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,8,7],[7,8,7,7,7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,7,7,7],[7,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"## What the grid is made of\n\nEvery non-background cell sits on a short **vertical line**. Most lines are pure 8. Exactly one line is partly 9: its top or bottom few cells are 9 and the rest are 8.\n\nThe line lengths form a ladder. Pair 1 has lengths 10, 8, 6, 4, 2. Pair 2 and pair 3 have similar sets of even lengths.\n\n## What changes\n\nCompare each input with its output, using the fact sheet.\n\n**Pair 1**\n- In the input, the line at x=9 (rows 3–6, length 4) has 9 on its top 2 cells.\n- In the output those 9s become 8.\n- The line at x=2 (rows 1–6, length **6**) gets 9 on its top **3** cells.\n\n**Pair 2**\n- In the input, the line at x=13 (rows 9–10, length 2) has 9 on its bottom 1 cell.\n- In the output that 9 becomes 8.\n- The line at x=1 (rows 1–4, length **4**) gets 9 on its bottom **2** cells.\n\n**Pair 3**\n- In the input, the line at x=9 (rows 0–7, length 8) has 9 on its bottom 4 cells.\n- In the output those 9s become 8.\n- The line at x=14 (rows 0–9, length **10**) gets 9 on its bottom **5** cells.\n\n## The rule\n\nTreat the 9 as a marker that climbs one step up the ladder of lengths:\n\n1. Find the line that contains 9. Call its length L, its number of 9 cells k, and note which end the 9s are on (top or bottom).\n2. Recolour that line's 9s back to 8.\n3. Find the line whose length is L+2.\n4. Recolour k+1 cells of that line to 9, at the same end.\n\nAll three pairs fit this rule exactly. A line is defined as a vertically connected run of 8/9 cells. In pair 2, the column x=1 holds two separate runs: rows 1–4 (length 4) and rows 7–12 (length 6). Only the length-4 run is the target.\n\n## Test\n\n- The 9s are on the line at x=1, rows 10–15 (length 6). The 9s are its top 3 cells, rows 10–12.\n- Those cells revert to 8.\n- The length-8 line is at x=7, rows 1–8. Its top 4 cells, rows 1–4, become 9.\n\nThe column x=7 also contains a separate run at rows 10–11. Because it is not connected to rows 1–8, it is not the target.\n\n## Program\n\nThe program builds a mask of all 8/9 cells and splits it into connected components (no diagonals), so each component is one vertical line. It then applies the four steps above. It emits a checkpoint after each of the two edits: the reverted 9 line, then the newly painted segment.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    lines = components(g != bg)\n    src = None\n    for c in lines:\n        if any(g[y, x] == 9 for y, x in c):\n            src = sorted(c)\n            break\n    if src is None:\n        emit(g, \"No 9 marker found; nothing to change.\")\n        return g\n    L = len(src)\n    k = sum(1 for y, x in src if g[y, x] == 9)\n    top = g[src[0]] == 9\n    for y, x in src:\n        g[y, x] = 8\n    emit(g, f\"The 9 marker ({k} cells, at the {'top' if top else 'bottom'}) on the length-{L} line reverts to 8.\")\n    tgt = None\n    for c in lines:\n        if len(c) == L + 2:\n            tgt = sorted(c)\n            break\n    if tgt is None:\n        emit(g, \"No line of length L+2 exists.\")\n        return g\n    seg = tgt[:k + 1] if top else tgt[-(k + 1):]\n    for y, x in seg:\n        g[y, x] = 9\n    emit(g, f\"The marker moves to the length-{L+2} line and grows to {k+1} cells at the same end.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The program builds a mask of all 8/9 cells and splits it into connected components (no diagonals), so each component is one vertical line."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Recolour that line's 9s back to 8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Recolour k+1 cells of that line to 9, at the same end."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Call its length L, its number of 9 cells k, and note which end the 9s are on (top or bottom)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"341122a07dcbdb21e95f7fcef21b547f54ad9b92e52ced06b6424f79785fd6d3","task_sha256":"7521bf234228b16361eab13686fd3e53c8177c49e10146bcbb42926c564096cb","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
